<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Admiral Peary asked for a same-day visit because at his daily foot check this morning, using the mirror as he was taught at intake, he found a blister on the end of his left forefoot, over the stump where his toes were amputated long ago. Two days ago he wore, for a long walk, a pair of boots he had bought before the winter and not yet broken in; he felt nothing at the time because of the numbness in his feet. There is no pain, redness spreading up the foot, discharge or fever. He finished the seven loading injections nine days ago and had his first weekly injection two days ago. He has not fallen. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Found this morning; unbroken boots worn two days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>End of the left forefoot, over the amputation stump</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>About two days</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>A fluid-filled blister</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Painless because of the numbness</td></tr><tr><td>Timing</td><td>After one long walk in boots not yet broken in</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Neuropathy from vitamin B12 deficiency; old toe amputations</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Old boots back on since this morning</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>No spreading redness, discharge, fever or chills</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

