    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 1919-02-03; see the Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General</td><td>Well; temperature 36.7 °C, pulse 88, blood pressure 124/70</td></tr><tr><td>Skin</td><td>A tense blister 1.5 by 1 cm with clear fluid over the end of the left forefoot stump beneath the second metatarsal head; roof intact; a rim of pinkness under 0.5 cm; no warmth, swelling, discharge or lymphangitic streaking; right foot intact, with a callus under the first metatarsal head</td></tr><tr><td>Cardiovascular</td><td>Dorsalis pedis and posterior tibial pulses present in both feet; capillary refill normal</td></tr><tr><td>Neurological</td><td>Monofilament felt at 3 of 10 sites on the left forefoot</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

