  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Fatigue, breathlessness on exertion, pallor with a lemon-yellow tinge, a sore tongue, and numbness and unsteadiness in the feet over about four months, with a macrocytic anemia, low white cells and platelets, a low vitamin B12 and a high methylmalonic acid; cause under evaluation with a hematology consultation</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>D51.9</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to the documented pernicious anemia of his last years; superseded when the consultation confirmed pernicious anemia.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Pernicious anemia (autoimmune gastritis with intrinsic factor antibodies), with severe vitamin B12 deficiency; synthetic modern diagnosis linked to the documented cause of his death</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>D51.0</td><td>S — Synthetic modern diagnosis made at the consultation, anchored to his documented death from pernicious anemia; the timing and course in the modern episode are synthetic.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-3">
    <td>Subacute combined degeneration of the spinal cord with peripheral neuropathy from vitamin B12 deficiency: loss of vibration and joint position sense in the feet, absent ankle jerks, brisk knee jerks and a positive Romberg test</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>G32.0</td><td>S — Synthetic neurological complication; not a claim about his real nerves.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Absence of the second to fifth toes of the right foot after frostbite and amputation in early middle age; healed stumps; callus under the first metatarsal head</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
