<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Blister on the left forefoot (S90.822A)</content>. A friction blister from unbroken boots in an insensate forefoot over an old amputation stump, found early by his daily check; no infection, and good circulation. Without protection, a blister like this can become an ulcer. [S]<list><item>Clean; leave the roof intact; a non-adherent dressing changed daily.</item><item>No unfitted boots; extra-depth shoes with toe fillers and a soft insole.</item><item>Podiatry visit moved forward to this week.</item><item>Return the same day for redness, warmth, swelling, discharge, a smell or fever; no antibiotics now.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subacute combined degeneration (G32.0)</content>. Sensory loss in the feet explains why the blister went unnoticed. [S]<list><item>Continue the daily foot checks and weekly injections.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Guidelines for the diagnosis and treatment of cobalamin and folate disorders (2014); Guidelines on the prevention of foot ulcers in persons with diabetes (IWGDF 2023 update) (2023)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Podiatry this week. Wound check at the five-week review, or sooner as above. Next scheduled visit 1919-02-17: five-week review on the day of upper endoscopy and colonoscopy: blood count, nerves, falls and feet. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
